<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Same markup as fields:</strong> wrap the select in
        <code>&lt;label class="fl-field"&gt;</code> with
        <code>fl-field__label</code> and optional <code>fl-field__help</code>.
        The class <code>fl-field__input</code> is the only select-specific
        class needed — <code>select.fl-field__input</code> switches on the
        chevron automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>All field states compose:</strong> <code>fl-field--filled</code>
        (tint fill + bottom indicator), <code>fl-field--error</code> /
        <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> (red border + red helper), and the
        native <code>disabled</code> attribute (dimmed box, chevron kept).</li>
    <li><strong>The popup is native:</strong> opening it draws a
        browser/OS-styled list. Closed-control styling is what the CSS
        guarantees; open-menu styling is platform behavior and differs
        between browsers — this is documented, not hidden.</li>
    <li><strong>Selected value renders as text</strong> — style it with the
        default body size/weight; don't restyle per-state, the platform
        repaints it on change.</li>
    <li><strong>Option styling is not supported</strong> —
        <code>&lt;option&gt;</code> elements are mostly unstyleable by
        design; keep their content plain text.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The wrapping label names the control natively; no
        <code>aria-label</code> needed when
        <code>fl-field__label</code> is present.</li>
    <li>The native select is one of the best-supported controls for
        assistive tech — announced name, role, value, and expanded state
        come from the platform.</li>
    <li>Keep the first option meaningful on optional fields ("Select a
        country" reads fine; "—" does not) and mark genuinely required
        selects with <code>required</code> so the platform validates.</li>
    <li>Validation errors: set <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> (which the
        CSS keys off) and put the reason in <code>fl-field__help</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

